IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `aia-core`
IMPORT `aia-timeline`
IMPORT `P6-art-51-52`

-- P6-art-55-56: Chapter V Sections 3 and 4, Article 55 (obligations of providers of general-purpose AI models with systemic risk) and Article 56 (codes of practice)
-- (Regulation (EU) 2024/1689 as amended by Regulation (EU) 2026/1744; the consolidated text of 27.7.2026 is a rendering with no legal effect).
-- Article 55 was not changed by the Omnibus. Article 56(6) was replaced by it (the passage marked M1 REPLACED): both texts are encoded, each in its own function with no date and no gate, and a dispatcher
-- chooses by `Omnibus Art 4 the version in force`. Chapter V applies from 2 August 2025, BEFORE the Omnibus (27 July 2026), so both versions are reachable through the dispatcher
-- (unlike Article 50(7), whose group begins after the Omnibus).
-- Layer 1: the law, objectively. Every function takes `the date asked` first. NOTHING is "not covered" (NOTHING-kind); JUST FALSE is the text's own no (FALSE-kind); JUST TRUE says the rule, duty or power arises.
-- A provider's duty passes the gate `Art 51 the obligations of the provider of the model are owed on the date asked` and, for Article 55, applies to a model with systemic risk only; the powers and duties of the
-- Commission, the AI Office and the Board pass the group only (fork F-111-3-scope).

DECLARE `Art 55 act` IS ONE OF
    `Art 55(1)(a) perform model evaluation in accordance with standardised protocols and tools reflecting the state of the art`
    `Art 55(1)(b) assess and mitigate possible systemic risks at Union level`
    `Art 55(1)(c) keep track of, document, and report relevant information about serious incidents and possible corrective measures`
    `Art 55(1)(d) ensure an adequate level of cybersecurity protection for the model and the physical infrastructure of the model`
    `Art 55(2) demonstrate alternative adequate means of compliance for assessment by the Commission`

DECLARE `Art 56 act` IS ONE OF
    `Art 56(1) encourage and facilitate the drawing up of codes of practice at Union level`
    `Art 56(2) aim to ensure that the codes of practice cover at least the obligations provided for in Articles 53 and 55`
    `Art 56(4) aim to ensure that the codes of practice clearly set out their specific objectives and take due account of the needs and interests of all interested parties`
    `Art 56(5) aim to ensure that participants to the codes of practice report regularly to the AI Office`
    `Art 56(6) monitor and evaluate the achievement of the objectives of the codes of practice`
    `Art 56(6) assess whether the codes of practice cover the obligations provided for in Articles 53 and 55`
    `Art 56(6) publish the assessment of the adequacy of the codes of practice`
    `Art 56(8) encourage and facilitate the review and adaptation of the codes of practice`
    `Art 56(8) assist in the assessment of available standards`
    `Art 56(9) take the necessary steps, including inviting providers pursuant to paragraph 7`

§ `Article 55: the gate of a provider of a model with systemic risk`

-- "providers of general-purpose AI models with systemic risk shall": the duties of Article 55 reach a provider whose model is classified under Article 51 (the seam S5 gives the BOOLEAN), in addition
-- to the gate of every provider of a general-purpose AI model.
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the model` IS AN `AI model`
      `the model is a general-purpose AI model` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the model is a general-purpose AI model with systemic risk` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 55 the obligations of the provider of a model with systemic risk are owed on the date asked` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `Art 51 the obligations of the provider of the model are owed on the date asked` `the date asked` `the model` `the model is a general-purpose AI model` EQUALS NOTHING
            THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter V applies from the date Art 113 gives, to a general-purpose AI model, and Art 111(3) can give its provider until 2 August 2027
        IF NOT `the model is a general-purpose AI model with systemic risk`
            THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "providers of general-purpose AI models with systemic risk shall"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§ `Article 55(1), point (a): model evaluation`

-- "perform model evaluation in accordance with standardised protocols and tools reflecting the state of the art, including conducting and documenting adversarial testing of the model with a view to identifying
-- and mitigating systemic risks". The adversarial testing after "including" is read as part of what the provider must do (fork F-55-1-a-including; the other reading: an illustration that adds no element).
-- src:816 | 1. In addition to the obligations listed in Articles 53 and 54, providers of general-purpose AI models with systemic risk shall:
-- src:817 | (a) perform model evaluation in accordance with standardised protocols and tools reflecting the state of the art, including conducting and documenting adversarial testing of the model with a view to identifying and mitigating systemic risks;
@ref Art 55(1)(a) (src:816-817)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the model` IS AN `AI model`
      `the model is a general-purpose AI model` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the model is a general-purpose AI model with systemic risk` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 55(1)(a) the provider must perform model evaluation` MEANS
    `Art 55 the obligations of the provider of a model with systemic risk are owed on the date asked` `the date asked` `the model` `the model is a general-purpose AI model` `the model is a general-purpose AI model with systemic risk`

-- src:817 | (a) perform model evaluation in accordance with standardised protocols and tools reflecting the state of the art, including conducting and documenting adversarial testing of the model with a view to identifying and mitigating systemic risks;
@ref Art 55(1)(a) (what the evaluation must be) (src:817)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the model` IS AN `AI model`
      `the model is a general-purpose AI model` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the model is a general-purpose AI model with systemic risk` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provider has performed model evaluation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the evaluation is in accordance with standardised protocols and tools reflecting the state of the art` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provider has conducted adversarial testing of the model` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provider has documented the adversarial testing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the adversarial testing is with a view to identifying and mitigating systemic risks` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 55(1)(a) the model evaluation is what the point requires` MEANS
    IF `Art 55(1)(a) the provider must perform model evaluation` `the date asked` `the model` `the model is a general-purpose AI model` `the model is a general-purpose AI model with systemic risk` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST (    `the provider has performed model evaluation`
               AND `the evaluation is in accordance with standardised protocols and tools reflecting the state of the art`
               AND `the provider has conducted adversarial testing of the model`
               AND `the provider has documented the adversarial testing`
               AND `the adversarial testing is with a view to identifying and mitigating systemic risks`)
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "providers of general-purpose AI models with systemic risk shall: (a) perform model evaluation in accordance with standardised protocols and tools ..., including conducting and documenting adversarial testing" (a bare "shall" not done, taken case by case)
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the point speaks of the provider who is bound by it

@ref Art 55(1)(a) (the duty; no time limit and no consequence in the text)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the model` IS AN `AI model`
      `the model is a general-purpose AI model` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the model is a general-purpose AI model with systemic risk` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Role `Art 55 act`
`Art 55(1)(a) the provider's duty to perform model evaluation` MEANS
    IF `Art 55(1)(a) the provider must perform model evaluation` `the date asked` `the model` `the model is a general-purpose AI model` `the model is a general-purpose AI model with systemic risk` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN PARTY Provider
         MUST `Art 55(1)(a) perform model evaluation in accordance with standardised protocols and tools reflecting the state of the art`
         -- no time limit and no consequence in the text (listed in NOTES.md, Rules with no breach path)
    ELSE FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed on these facts

§ `Article 55(1), point (b): assessing and mitigating systemic risks`

-- "assess and mitigate possible systemic risks at Union level, including their sources, that may stem from the development, the placing on the market, or the use of general-purpose AI models with systemic risk".
-- "Including their sources" is read as part of what is assessed and mitigated (fork F-55-1-b-including).
-- src:818 | (b) assess and mitigate possible systemic risks at Union level, including their sources, that may stem from the development, the placing on the market, or the use of general-purpose AI models with systemic risk;
@ref Art 55(1)(b) (src:818)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the model` IS AN `AI model`
      `the model is a general-purpose AI model` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the model is a general-purpose AI model with systemic risk` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 55(1)(b) the provider must assess and mitigate possible systemic risks at Union level` MEANS
    `Art 55 the obligations of the provider of a model with systemic risk are owed on the date asked` `the date asked` `the model` `the model is a general-purpose AI model` `the model is a general-purpose AI model with systemic risk`

-- src:818 | (b) assess and mitigate possible systemic risks at Union level, including their sources, that may stem from the development, the placing on the market, or the use of general-purpose AI models with systemic risk;
@ref Art 55(1)(b) (what the assessment and mitigation must be) (src:818)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the model` IS AN `AI model`
      `the model is a general-purpose AI model` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the model is a general-purpose AI model with systemic risk` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provider has assessed the possible systemic risks at Union level` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provider has mitigated the possible systemic risks at Union level` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the assessment and the mitigation include the sources of the risks` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 55(1)(b) the assessment and mitigation of the systemic risks are what the point requires` MEANS
    IF `Art 55(1)(b) the provider must assess and mitigate possible systemic risks at Union level` `the date asked` `the model` `the model is a general-purpose AI model` `the model is a general-purpose AI model with systemic risk` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST (    `the provider has assessed the possible systemic risks at Union level`
               AND `the provider has mitigated the possible systemic risks at Union level`
               AND `the assessment and the mitigation include the sources of the risks`)
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "providers of general-purpose AI models with systemic risk shall: (b) assess and mitigate possible systemic risks at Union level, including their sources" (a bare "shall" not done, taken case by case)
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the point speaks of the provider who is bound by it

@ref Art 55(1)(b) (the duty; no time limit and no consequence in the text)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the model` IS AN `AI model`
      `the model is a general-purpose AI model` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the model is a general-purpose AI model with systemic risk` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Role `Art 55 act`
`Art 55(1)(b) the provider's duty to assess and mitigate possible systemic risks` MEANS
    IF `Art 55(1)(b) the provider must assess and mitigate possible systemic risks at Union level` `the date asked` `the model` `the model is a general-purpose AI model` `the model is a general-purpose AI model with systemic risk` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN PARTY Provider
         MUST `Art 55(1)(b) assess and mitigate possible systemic risks at Union level`
         -- no time limit and no consequence in the text (listed in NOTES.md, Rules with no breach path)
    ELSE FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed on these facts

§ `Article 55(1), point (c): serious incidents`

-- "keep track of, document, and report, without undue delay, to the AI Office and, as appropriate, to national competent authorities, relevant information about serious incidents and possible corrective measures
-- to address them". The duty has the serious incident as its object: with no serious incident it has none (NOTHING). "Without undue delay" has no number of days: it is a plain input, and the rule has no deadline.
-- The incident is a "serious incident" as Article 3(49) defines it: the seat computes that with the keel's function and passes the answer in.
-- src:819 | (c) keep track of, document, and report, without undue delay, to the AI Office and, as appropriate, to national competent authorities, relevant information about serious incidents and possible corrective measures to address them;
@ref Art 55(1)(c) (src:819)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the model` IS AN `AI model`
      `the model is a general-purpose AI model` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the model is a general-purpose AI model with systemic risk` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there has been a serious incident` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 55(1)(c) the provider must keep track of, document, and report relevant information about serious incidents and possible corrective measures` MEANS
    IF `Art 55 the obligations of the provider of a model with systemic risk are owed on the date asked` `the date asked` `the model` `the model is a general-purpose AI model` `the model is a general-purpose AI model with systemic risk` EQUALS NOTHING
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter V applies from the date Art 113 gives, to a provider of a model with systemic risk, and Art 111(3) can give it until 2 August 2027
    ELSE IF `there has been a serious incident`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "relevant information about serious incidents": the duty has no object without one

-- src:819 | (c) keep track of, document, and report, without undue delay, to the AI Office and, as appropriate, to national competent authorities, relevant information about serious incidents and possible corrective measures to address them;
@ref Art 55(1)(c) (what the tracking and reporting must be) (src:819)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the model` IS AN `AI model`
      `the model is a general-purpose AI model` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the model is a general-purpose AI model with systemic risk` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there has been a serious incident` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provider keeps track of and documents the relevant information about the serious incident and possible corrective measures` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provider has reported the information to the AI Office` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report was made without undue delay` IS A BOOLEAN
      `reporting to the national competent authorities is appropriate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provider has reported the information to the national competent authorities` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 55(1)(c) the tracking, documenting and reporting are what the point requires` MEANS
    IF `Art 55(1)(c) the provider must keep track of, document, and report relevant information about serious incidents and possible corrective measures` `the date asked` `the model` `the model is a general-purpose AI model` `the model is a general-purpose AI model with systemic risk` `there has been a serious incident` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST (    `the provider keeps track of and documents the relevant information about the serious incident and possible corrective measures`
               AND `the provider has reported the information to the AI Office`
               AND `the report was made without undue delay`
               AND ((NOT `reporting to the national competent authorities is appropriate`) OR `the provider has reported the information to the national competent authorities`))
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "keep track of, document, and report, without undue delay, to the AI Office and, as appropriate, to national competent authorities" (a bare "shall" not done, taken case by case)
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the point speaks of the provider who is bound by it, on the occasion of a serious incident

@ref Art 55(1)(c) (the duty; no time limit and no consequence in the text)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the model` IS AN `AI model`
      `the model is a general-purpose AI model` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the model is a general-purpose AI model with systemic risk` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there has been a serious incident` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Role `Art 55 act`
`Art 55(1)(c) the provider's duty to keep track of, document and report serious incidents` MEANS
    IF `Art 55(1)(c) the provider must keep track of, document, and report relevant information about serious incidents and possible corrective measures` `the date asked` `the model` `the model is a general-purpose AI model` `the model is a general-purpose AI model with systemic risk` `there has been a serious incident` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN PARTY Provider
         MUST `Art 55(1)(c) keep track of, document, and report relevant information about serious incidents and possible corrective measures`
         -- no time limit and no consequence in the text: "without undue delay" has no number of days (listed in NOTES.md, Rules with no breach path)
    ELSE FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed on these facts

