§ `Article 55(2): codes of practice, harmonised standards, and alternative means`

-- The three sentences are those of Article 53(4), for the obligations of paragraph 1 of Article 55 and for providers of models with systemic risk; the readings taken are the same (forks F-55-2-until, F-55-2-presumption, F-55-2-or).
-- src:821 | 2. Providers of general-purpose AI models with systemic risk may rely on codes of practice within the meaning of Article 56 to demonstrate compliance with the obligations set out in paragraph 1 of this Article, until a harmonised standard is published. Compliance with European harmonised standards grants providers the presumption of conformity to the extent that those standards cover those obligations. Providers of general-purpose AI models with systemic risks who do not adhere to an approved code of practice or do not comply with a European harmonised standard shall demonstrate alternative adequate means of compliance for assessment by the Commission.
@ref Art 55(2) first sentence (src:821)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the model is a general-purpose AI model with systemic risk` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the code of practice is within the meaning of Article 56` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a harmonised standard covering the obligations has been published` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 55(2) the provider may rely on a code of practice to demonstrate compliance with the obligations set out in paragraph 1` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`Art 51 the group applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
            THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter V applies from the date Art 113 gives
        IF NOT `the model is a general-purpose AI model with systemic risk`
            THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Providers of general-purpose AI models with systemic risk may rely"
        IF NOT `the code of practice is within the meaning of Article 56`
            THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "codes of practice within the meaning of Article 56"
        IF `a harmonised standard covering the obligations has been published`
            THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may rely on codes of practice ... until a harmonised standard is published" (the "until" bar has been reached)
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:821 | 2. Providers of general-purpose AI models with systemic risk may rely on codes of practice within the meaning of Article 56 to demonstrate compliance with the obligations set out in paragraph 1 of this Article, until a harmonised standard is published. Compliance with European harmonised standards grants providers the presumption of conformity to the extent that those standards cover those obligations. Providers of general-purpose AI models with systemic risks who do not adhere to an approved code of practice or do not comply with a European harmonised standard shall demonstrate alternative adequate means of compliance for assessment by the Commission.
@ref Art 55(2) second sentence (src:821)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the model is a general-purpose AI model with systemic risk` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provider complies with a European harmonised standard` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that standard covers the obligation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 55(2) the provider is presumed to conform with the obligation to the extent that a European harmonised standard covers it` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`Art 51 the group applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
            THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter V applies from the date Art 113 gives
        IF NOT `the model is a general-purpose AI model with systemic risk`
            THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Compliance with European harmonised standards grants providers" of models with systemic risk the presumption
        IF `the provider complies with a European harmonised standard` AND `that standard covers the obligation`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the presumption is granted for compliance with a standard "to the extent that those standards cover those obligations"

