         -- no time limit and no consequence in the text (listed in NOTES.md, Rules with no breach path)
    ELSE FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed on these facts

§ `Article 56(2): what the codes of practice are to cover`

-- "The AI Office and the Board shall aim to ensure that the codes of practice cover at least the obligations provided for in Articles 53 and 55, including the following issues: (a) ... (d)".
-- The duty is to aim; the second function says whether the codes cover what the paragraph aims at. The issues after "including" are read as part of it (fork F-56-2-including).
-- src:828 | 2. The AI Office and the Board shall aim to ensure that the codes of practice cover at least the obligations provided for in Articles 53 and 55, including the following issues:
-- src:829 | (a) the means to ensure that the information referred to in Article 53(1), points (a) and (b), is kept up to date in light of market and technological developments;
-- src:830 | (b) the adequate level of detail for the summary about the content used for training;
-- src:831 | (c) the identification of the type and nature of the systemic risks at Union level, including their sources, where appropriate;
-- src:832 | (d) the measures, procedures and modalities for the assessment and management of the systemic risks at Union level, including the documentation thereof, which shall be proportionate to the risks, take into consideration their severity and probability and take into account the specific challenges of tackling those risks in light of the possible ways in which such risks may emerge and materialise along the AI value chain.
@ref Art 56(2) (src:828-832)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 56(2) the AI Office and the Board must aim to ensure that the codes of practice cover at least the obligations provided for in Articles 53 and 55` MEANS
    IF `Art 51 the group applies on the date asked` `the date asked`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter V applies from the date Art 113 gives

-- src:828 | 2. The AI Office and the Board shall aim to ensure that the codes of practice cover at least the obligations provided for in Articles 53 and 55, including the following issues:
-- src:829 | (a) the means to ensure that the information referred to in Article 53(1), points (a) and (b), is kept up to date in light of market and technological developments;
-- src:830 | (b) the adequate level of detail for the summary about the content used for training;
-- src:831 | (c) the identification of the type and nature of the systemic risks at Union level, including their sources, where appropriate;
-- src:832 | (d) the measures, procedures and modalities for the assessment and management of the systemic risks at Union level, including the documentation thereof, which shall be proportionate to the risks, take into consideration their severity and probability and take into account the specific challenges of tackling those risks in light of the possible ways in which such risks may emerge and materialise along the AI value chain.
@ref Art 56(2) (what the codes must cover) (src:828-832)
