§ `Article 56(6): monitoring, assessing and publishing (both versions; the Omnibus replaced the paragraph)`

-- VERSION as enacted (base text): "The AI Office and the Board shall regularly monitor and evaluate the achievement of the objectives of the codes of practice ... The AI Office and the Board shall assess whether the codes of
-- practice cover the obligations provided for in Articles 53 and 55, and shall regularly monitor and evaluate the achievement of their objectives. They shall publish their assessment of the adequacy of the codes of practice."
-- VERSION as amended: "The Commission and the Board shall regularly monitor and evaluate ... The Commission, taking utmost account of the opinion of the Board, shall assess whether the codes of practice cover the
-- obligations ..., and shall regularly monitor and evaluate the achievement of their objectives. The Commission shall publish its assessment of the adequacy of the codes of practice."
-- The text as enacted had a second subparagraph, a power of the Commission to approve a code by implementing act; the replaced paragraph has none (the passage was replaced, and the approval power is not in the text as amended).
-- src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:1391 | 6. The AI Office and the Board shall regularly monitor and evaluate the achievement of the objectives of the codes of practice by the participants and their contribution to the proper application of this Regulation. The AI Office and the Board shall assess whether the codes of practice cover the obligations provided for in Articles 53 and 55, and shall regularly monitor and evaluate the achievement of their objectives. They shall publish their assessment of the adequacy of the codes of practice.
-- src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:1392 | The Commission may, by way of an implementing act, approve a code of practice and give it a general validity within the Union. That implementing act shall be adopted in accordance with the examination procedure referred to in Article 98(2).
@ref Art 56(6) as enacted (src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:1391-1392)
GIVETH A `Art 51 official`
`Art 56(6) as enacted the official who must assess whether the codes of practice cover the obligations and publish the assessment` MEANS `Art 51 the AI Office`

-- src:837 | 6. The Commission and the Board shall regularly monitor and evaluate the achievement of the objectives of the codes of practice by the participants and their contribution to the proper application of this Regulation. The Commission, taking utmost account of the opinion of the Board, shall assess whether the codes of practice cover the obligations provided for in Articles 53 and 55, and shall regularly monitor and evaluate the achievement of their objectives. The Commission shall publish its assessment of the adequacy of the codes of practice.
@ref Art 56(6) as amended (src:837)
GIVETH A `Art 51 official`
`Art 56(6) as amended the official who must assess whether the codes of practice cover the obligations and publish the assessment` MEANS `Art 51 the Commission`

-- Dispatcher. NOTHING before Chapter V applies (2 August 2025). The group applies before the Omnibus, so both branches are reached: the AI Office until 26 July 2026, the Commission from 27 July 2026.
@ref Art 56(6), both versions
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE `Art 51 official`
`Art 56(6) the official who must assess whether the codes of practice cover the obligations and publish the assessment` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Art 51 the group applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter V applies from the date Art 113 gives
    ELSE CONSIDER `Omnibus Art 4 the version in force` `the date asked`
         WHEN `as enacted` THEN JUST (`Art 56(6) as enacted the official who must assess whether the codes of practice cover the obligations and publish the assessment`)  -- VERSION as enacted
         WHEN `as amended` THEN JUST (`Art 56(6) as amended the official who must assess whether the codes of practice cover the obligations and publish the assessment`)  -- VERSION as amended

@ref Art 56(6), both versions (the duty to assess and publish; no time limit and no consequence in the text)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Art 51 official` `Art 56 act`
`Art 56(6) the duty to assess whether the codes of practice cover the obligations and to publish the assessment` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Art 51 the group applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed: the group does not apply on the date asked
    ELSE CONSIDER `Omnibus Art 4 the version in force` `the date asked`
         WHEN `as enacted` THEN                                     -- VERSION as enacted
             PARTY `Art 51 the AI Office`
             MUST `Art 56(6) assess whether the codes of practice cover the obligations provided for in Articles 53 and 55`
         WHEN `as amended` THEN                                     -- VERSION as amended
             PARTY `Art 51 the Commission`
             MUST `Art 56(6) assess whether the codes of practice cover the obligations provided for in Articles 53 and 55`

@ref Art 56(6), both versions (the duty to publish the assessment; no time limit and no consequence in the text)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Art 51 official` `Art 56 act`
`Art 56(6) the duty to publish the assessment of the adequacy of the codes of practice` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Art 51 the group applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed: the group does not apply on the date asked
    ELSE CONSIDER `Omnibus Art 4 the version in force` `the date asked`
         WHEN `as enacted` THEN                                     -- VERSION as enacted
             PARTY `Art 51 the AI Office`
             MUST `Art 56(6) publish the assessment of the adequacy of the codes of practice`
         WHEN `as amended` THEN                                     -- VERSION as amended
             PARTY `Art 51 the Commission`
             MUST `Art 56(6) publish the assessment of the adequacy of the codes of practice`

-- The Board: in both versions it monitors and evaluates (as enacted it also assesses and publishes with the AI Office; as amended it gives the opinion the Commission takes utmost account of, which is not
-- stated as a duty). The Board's duty to monitor and evaluate is the same in both texts: one function, gated by the group.
-- src:837 | 6. The Commission and the Board shall regularly monitor and evaluate the achievement of the objectives of the codes of practice by the participants and their contribution to the proper application of this Regulation. The Commission, taking utmost account of the opinion of the Board, shall assess whether the codes of practice cover the obligations provided for in Articles 53 and 55, and shall regularly monitor and evaluate the achievement of their objectives. The Commission shall publish its assessment of the adequacy of the codes of practice.
@ref Art 56(6) the Board's duty to monitor and evaluate, both versions (src:837)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Art 51 official` `Art 56 act`
