    IF `Art 51 the group applies on the date asked` `the date asked`
    THEN PARTY `Art 51 the Board`
         MUST `Art 56(6) monitor and evaluate the achievement of the objectives of the codes of practice`
         -- no time limit and no consequence in the text (listed in NOTES.md, Rules with no breach path)
    ELSE FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed: the group does not apply on the date asked

-- As enacted, second subparagraph: "The Commission may, by way of an implementing act, approve a code of practice and give it a general validity within the Union." An unconditional power; the text as
-- amended has no such power, so the as-amended branch answers NOTHING (silent).
-- src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:1392 | The Commission may, by way of an implementing act, approve a code of practice and give it a general validity within the Union. That implementing act shall be adopted in accordance with the examination procedure referred to in Article 98(2).
@ref Art 56(6) as enacted, second subparagraph (the power to approve a code) (src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:1392)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 56(6) as enacted the Commission may approve a code of practice by an implementing act` MEANS JUST TRUE

@ref Art 56(6), both versions (the power to approve a code)
