§ `Article 56(9): the date by which the codes are ready, and the Commission's fall-back`

-- First subparagraph, first sentence: "Codes of practice shall be ready at the latest by 2 May 2025." The text names no party. The date precedes the day Chapter V begins to apply (2 August 2025), so the function is
-- gated by the group and answers NOTHING for any date asked before 2 August 2025; from then on it judges the date the codes were ready against 2 May 2025 (a finding in NOTES.md; fork F-56-9-date).
-- A period the text fixes in its own words: a later date is JUST FALSE (periods ruling, rule (a)).
-- src:841 | 9. Codes of practice shall be ready at the latest by 2 May 2025. The AI Office shall take the necessary steps, including inviting providers pursuant to paragraph 7.
@ref Art 56(9) first subparagraph, first sentence (src:841)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the date the codes of practice were ready` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 56(9) the codes of practice were ready at the latest by 2 May 2025` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Art 51 the group applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter V applies from the date Art 113 gives (2 August 2025, after the 2 May 2025 of this sentence)
    ELSE JUST (`the date the codes of practice were ready` AT MOST Date 2 5 2025)
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Codes of practice shall be ready at the latest by 2 May 2025" (a period the text fixes in its own words: a later date is no)

-- Second sentence: "The AI Office shall take the necessary steps, including inviting providers pursuant to paragraph 7."
-- src:841 | 9. Codes of practice shall be ready at the latest by 2 May 2025. The AI Office shall take the necessary steps, including inviting providers pursuant to paragraph 7.
@ref Art 56(9) first subparagraph, second sentence (src:841)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 56(9) the AI Office must take the necessary steps, including inviting providers pursuant to paragraph 7` MEANS
    IF `Art 51 the group applies on the date asked` `the date asked`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter V applies from the date Art 113 gives

@ref Art 56(9) first subparagraph, second sentence (the duty; no time limit and no consequence in the text)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Art 51 official` `Art 56 act`
`Art 56(9) the AI Office's duty to take the necessary steps` MEANS
    IF `Art 56(9) the AI Office must take the necessary steps, including inviting providers pursuant to paragraph 7` `the date asked` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN PARTY `Art 51 the AI Office`
         MUST `Art 56(9) take the necessary steps, including inviting providers pursuant to paragraph 7`
         -- no time limit and no consequence in the text: the second sentence has no date of its own (listed in NOTES.md, Rules with no breach path)
    ELSE FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed on these facts

-- Second subparagraph: "If, by 2 August 2025, a code of practice cannot be finalised, or if the AI Office deems it is not adequate following its assessment under paragraph 6 of this Article, the Commission may
-- provide, by means of implementing acts, common rules for the implementation of the obligations provided for in Articles 53 and 55, including the issues set out in paragraph 2". A "may" gated by "if": NOTHING when
-- neither limb holds (the grant ruling). The second limb speaks of an assessment by the AI Office under paragraph 6; as amended paragraph 6 gives the assessment to the Commission (a finding in NOTES.md):
-- the limb is kept as the plain fact it names, in both versions (fork F-56-9-ii).
-- src:842 | If, by 2 August 2025, a code of practice cannot be finalised, or if the AI Office deems it is not adequate following its assessment under paragraph 6 of this Article, the Commission may provide, by means of implementing acts, common rules for the implementation of the obligations provided for in Articles 53 and 55, including the issues set out in paragraph 2 of this Article. Those implementing acts shall be adopted in accordance with the examination procedure referred to in Article 98(2).
@ref Art 56(9) second subparagraph (src:842)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `a code of practice cannot be finalised by 2 August 2025` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the AI Office deems the code not adequate following its assessment under paragraph 6` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 56(9) the Commission may provide, by means of implementing acts, common rules for the implementation of the obligations provided for in Articles 53 and 55` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`Art 51 the group applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
            THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter V applies from the date Art 113 gives
        IF `a code of practice cannot be finalised by 2 August 2025` OR `the AI Office deems the code not adequate following its assessment under paragraph 6`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is given "If, by 2 August 2025, a code of practice cannot be finalised, or if the AI Office deems it is not adequate"
